# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Freelancey — Frontend (Web) Environment
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Next.js 15 App Router app (port 3000), deployed on Vercel.
# Backend variables live in backend/.env.example — keep them separate.
#
# Copy this file to frontend/.env for local development
# (`npm run dev` does this automatically on first run).
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars are inlined into the client bundle at build time —
# changing them requires a rebuild. Non-prefixed vars are server-only
# (server components / route handlers) and are never exposed to the browser.

# ── App URLs ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL = browser-facing API base URL (inlined at build time)
# API_URL             = server-side API base URL (server components/actions)
# WEB_URL             = canonical frontend origin (middleware domain detection)
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL="http://localhost:3001"
API_URL="http://localhost:3001"
WEB_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Authentication (Neon Auth — Managed Better Auth) ─────
# "Auth URL" from your Neon project's Auth tab (includes the project's
# db-name path segment). The auth proxy route (/api/auth/[...path])
# forwards requests here so the session cookie is first-party.
NEON_AUTH_BASE_URL=""
# Frontend-only. Signs the auth proxy's own first-party session cookies —
# not a Neon credential, generate with `openssl rand -base64 32` (min 32 chars).
NEON_AUTH_COOKIE_SECRET=""

# ── Analytics / Tracking (optional) ─────────────────────
# JSON array of script tags. Each object's keys become attributes on a <script> tag.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TRACKERS='[{"src":"https://umami.example.com/script.js","data-website-id":"your-id"}]'

# ── Error Reporting / Sentry (optional) ──────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://xxx@sentry.io/xxx  # Web app errors (client + SSR)
# SENTRY_DSN=https://xxx@sentry.io/xxx              # API server errors (if proxied)
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=sntrys_xxx                      # Source map uploads (build-time only)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_ENABLED=true
# SENTRY_ENABLED=true

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Production (Vercel — portal.groundwork.co.ke)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Set these directly in the Vercel project's Environment Variables — never
# commit real values to this file. NEXT_PUBLIC_* take effect on the next build.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL="https://portal-api.groundwork.co.ke"
#   API_URL="https://portal-api.groundwork.co.ke"   — used by server components
#   WEB_URL="https://portal.groundwork.co.ke"
#   NEON_AUTH_BASE_URL, NEON_AUTH_COOKIE_SECRET     — the auth proxy route (server-side only)
#   (plus NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_* / NEXT_PUBLIC_TRACKERS as needed)
#
# Never set NEON_AUTH_COOKIE_SECRET where it'd be exposed to the browser —
# it isn't NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed, so Next.js never bundles it into client JS.
